  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to essential lifesaving WASH and Health emergency interventions to vulnerable girls, boys, women, and men affected and displaced by the March-May 2024 seasonal floods in priority flood-affected counties of Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective is to provide essential lifesaving Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH) and health emergency interventions to vulnerable girls, boys, women, and men affected and displaced by the March-May 2024 seasonal floods in priority flood-affected counties of Kenya. UNICEF&apos;s WASH activities provide safe water, hygiene services, and sanitation to people in Homa Bay, Garissa, and Tana River counties. In partnership with the Kenya Red Cross and local health departments, UNICEF delivers integrated health services, including immunizations and reproductive care. Communication strategies raise awareness of preventive health measures to improve outcomes and reduce suffering. UNICEF targets 116,474 people, including 24,459 women, 8,153 men, and 582 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
